Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: propagate errored capture buffers to requests

VIDIOC_DQBUF can succeed while V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR reports a failed decode.
Mark the request failed instead of handing that storage to the output path.
Observed with an original stateless decoder returning a bounded hardware error.

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2decoder.c
@@ -1028,6 +1028,13 @@ gst_v4l2_decoder_dequeue_src (GstV4l2Decoder * self, guint32 * out_frame_num)
     return FALSE;
   }
 
+  if (buf.flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR) {
+    GST_ERROR_OBJECT (self, "Driver reported an error for picture buffer %u",
+        buf.index);
+    errno = EIO;
+    return FALSE;
+  }
+
   *out_frame_num = buf.timestamp.tv_usec + buf.timestamp.tv_sec * 1000000;
 
   GST_TRACE_OBJECT (self, "Dequeued picture buffer %i", buf.index);
